BT /F1 11 Tf 50 720 Td 14 TL
/F1 14 Tf (Chapter 2: Deadlock Handling and Banker's Algorithm) Tj /F1 11 Tf T*
(A deadlock occurs when a set of processes are blocked because each process is holding a resource and waiting for another resource held by another process.) Tj T*
(Four Coffman conditions must hold simultaneously for a deadlock to occur:) Tj T*
(1. Mutual Exclusion: At least one resource must be held in a non-shareable mode.) Tj T*
(2. Hold and Wait: A process must be holding at least one resource and waiting to acquire additional resources.) Tj T*
(3. No Preemption: Resources cannot be forcibly taken from a process.) Tj T*
(4. Circular Wait: A closed loop of processes exists where each process waits for a resource held by the next.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Banker's Algorithm:) Tj T*
(Developed by Edsger Dijkstra, the Banker's algorithm is a deadlock avoidance algorithm.) Tj T*
(It tests for safety by simulating resource allocation for maximum possible requests, and ensures the system remains in a safe state where a safe execution sequence exists for all processes.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
